{
  "name": "Send new federal grants for your field to Slack and Google Sheets every morning with SpecStream",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## New grants for your field, every morning\n\nEach morning at 7 this workflow asks SpecStream for open federal grants that fit your field and posts only the new ones to Slack, with the funder, the deadline and a link to the official listing. Every grant also goes to a Google Sheet, so you keep a log of what you've seen.\n\n### How it works\n1. **First run:** SpecStream finds every open grant that fits the request and logs them all.\n2. **Every run after that:** it continues the same list and asks only for grants the log doesn't hold yet. A morning with nothing new costs nothing and posts nothing.\n3. Each run is priced first. If the price is above your maximum, the workflow stops and tells you.\n\n### Set up (5 minutes)\n1. Get a free API key at [specstream.ai](https://specstream.ai) under **Agents & API**. New accounts get $10 of credit, no card.\n2. In n8n, create a **Bearer Auth** credential with the key and pick it in the six SpecStream HTTP nodes.\n3. Write your field in **Your grant search**, for example *Open federal grants for rural broadband*.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and pick the same empty sheet in **Read the grant log** and **Add to the grant log**.\n5. Connect Slack and pick a channel in **Post to Slack**. Run once by hand, then activate.\n\n### Price\n5¢ a grant, shown before anything runs. You pay only for new matches. The default maximum is $2.50 a morning.",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "37fe5049-93e5-52f4-b9c2-ef2ccbf17e50",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Your search and the log\nChange the request in **Your grant search**. To start a log for a different field, use a new empty sheet. **First run or new ones?** reads the log to see where the last run stopped.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 880,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "6a9a4ea7-f261-5403-8da3-6a8c1101ef24",
      "name": "Step 1",
